[TITLE]
LINK_OFFSETS=ELEVATION probe for the GeoPackage round trip.

Under ELEVATION the offsets in the file are ELEVATIONS, and the resolver
rewrites each as a depth above its node invert. C1 leaves J1 (invert 100) at
elevation 102, i.e. a depth of 2.

If the .gpkg stores the resolved DEPTH while still declaring
LINK_OFFSETS=ELEVATION, reopening subtracts the invert a second time
(2 - 100 = -98, clamped to 0) and the offset is destroyed.

[OPTIONS]
FLOW_UNITS           CFS
FLOW_ROUTING         DYNWAVE
LINK_OFFSETS         ELEVATION
START_DATE           01/01/2024
END_DATE             01/02/2024
REPORT_STEP          00:15:00
ROUTING_STEP         00:00:30

[JUNCTIONS]
;;Name  Elev   MaxDepth
J1      100.0  10.0
J2       98.0  10.0

[OUTFALLS]
;;Name  Elev  Type  Stage  Gated
O1       90.0 FREE         NO

[CONDUITS]
;;Name  From  To  Length  Rough  InOffset(elev)  OutOffset(elev)
C1      J1    J2  100.0   0.013  102.0           99.5
C2      J2    O1  100.0   0.013  98.5            90.0

[XSECTIONS]
C1  CIRCULAR  1.5  0  0  0  1
C2  CIRCULAR  1.5  0  0  0  1

[COORDINATES]
J1  0    0
J2  100  0
O1  200  0
